This version focuses on developing the redactable map, which is in fact JPanel (paintPanel in Window.java)
on which user will paint his tiles and units by mouseClicks.

Because map consists of different colors i need a way repaint a map which user is redacting after the window was
invalidated by size change or hide/show.
The solution to this problem is buffered image in which all maps paint actions will be duplicated and later used
in case of window invalidation to copy whole image on JPanel at once.

Here arises another issue there is a need
to separate paint instructions used for different cases and at the same tile it'll be better for the code
extendability to avoid usage of conditional statements. The idea is to use state pattern and for that purpose
interface PaintInstruction and class InstructedPaintPanel were created. paintInstruction is in fact "instructions"
of what exactly should be painted on JPanel. InstructedPaintPanel uses instruction object in its paintComponent
method to realise code inside PaintInstruction.

image buffer and instructed panel will be used together, because every paint action on the panel will be
duplicated on buffer, therefore there is a need to contain them in the class there painting they both will be
painted. There is two approaches for that inheritance and aggregation. Inheritance may give us more extendability
in the way that we can use this class in the place of instructed panel, however here arises the problem with
default paint instruction, which is supposed to be a buffer image coping, seeing that must be a way to set
default paint instruction to instructed panel. In case with inheritance with can create a method in new class
but that will destroy the purpose of us using inheritance, because we won't be able to use this new class as
instructed panel. We can set default instruction in paintComponent method, but this way it will be called every
time panel paints something or default paint set instruction can be place inside other paintInstruction classes,
this however will make them more complex and less reusable. For purpose of setting default instruction it is more
beneficial to use aggregation which still allows us to use different types of instructed panel inside it.

Tiles are painted by processing mouse click events in which we need coordinate of mouse click to determine in
which grid cell tile is need to be painted. (In this version tiles are painted outside grid).


Can create tiles

Created BufferedPaintPanelV2: paints in panel and buffer. I use agregation instead of inheritance because i
need a way to set default instruction, which should be hidden from outside to not bother in further development
and with inheritance i wouldn't know when to set default instruction back/

But the problem of setting default instruction still stands. Now BufferedPaintPanelV2 calls
SwingUtilities.invokeLater() for setting default instruction for every time instruction changes.